.\" Manual page for html2md.
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.TH HTML2MD 1 "September 2026" "html2md 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
html2md \- convert HTML documents to clean, readable Markdown
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B html2md
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIFILE\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B html2md
reads each
.I FILE
(or standard input when
.I FILE
is
.B \-
or absent) and writes GitHub Flavored Markdown or CommonMark to standard
output.
.PP
Input is parsed with the same error recovery rules as web browsers, so
malformed markup (unclosed or misnested tags, stray table content, unknown
elements) converts sensibly. Scripts, styles, forms, embedded objects,
comments and hidden elements are removed. Markdown syntax characters that
occur in text are escaped only where they would otherwise change the
meaning of the output.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Input and output"
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIFILE\fR
Write the result to
.I FILE
instead of standard output. Several inputs are concatenated, separated by
a blank line.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-output\-dir =\fIDIR\fR
Write each input file to
.IR DIR / NAME .md,
where
.I NAME
is the input's file name without its extension.
.I DIR
is created if it does not exist.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-encoding =\fINAME\fR
Decode the input as
.IR NAME :
utf\-8, windows\-1252, iso\-8859\-1 (latin1), iso\-8859\-15, us\-ascii,
utf\-16le or utf\-16be. By default the encoding is taken from a byte order
mark or a
.B <meta charset>
declaration; input that is not valid UTF\-8 is decoded as windows\-1252.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-base\-url =\fIURL\fR
Resolve relative link and image URLs against the absolute
.IR URL .
A
.B <base href>
in the document is honoured as well.
.SS "Content selection"
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-main
Keep only the main content: the
.B <main>
element, an element with
.BR role="main" ,
or a single
.BR <article> .
Navigation, search forms, and headers, footers and sidebars outside the
content are removed.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-select =\fISELECTOR\fR
Convert only elements matching the CSS
.IR SELECTOR ,
in document order.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude =\fISELECTOR\fR
Remove elements matching
.IR SELECTOR .
May be given several times.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-hidden
Keep elements hidden with the
.B hidden
attribute,
.BR aria\-hidden="true" ,
.B display:none
or
.BR visibility:hidden .
Collapsed accordion and disclosure panels are marked this way, so this
option is what converts their text.
.TP
.BR \-\-links =\fIMODE\fR
.B inline
(default) writes [text](url);
.B reference
writes [text][n] with the definitions at the end;
.B none
keeps only the link text.
.TP
.BR \-\-images =\fIMODE\fR
.B inline
(default) writes ![alt](src);
.B alt
keeps only the alternative text;
.B none
drops images.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-data\-uris
Keep images whose source is an inline
.B data:
URI (dropped by default because of their size).
.SS "Markdown style"
.TP
.BR \-\-flavor =\fINAME\fR
.B gfm
(default) uses GitHub Flavored Markdown tables, strikethrough and task
lists.
.B commonmark
emits strict CommonMark and falls back to inline HTML for tables and
strikethrough.
.TP
.BR \-\-heading\-style =\fISTYLE\fR
.B atx
(default, "# Title") or
.B setext
(underlined level 1 and 2 headings).
.TP
.BR \-\-bullet =\fICHAR\fR
Bullet list marker:
.B \-
(default),
.B *
or
.BR + .
.TP
.BR \-\-emphasis =\fICHAR\fR ", " \-\-strong =\fICHAR\fR
Emphasis delimiters:
.B *
(default) or
.BR _ .
Where the preferred delimiter would not be recognised by a Markdown parser
(for example in "**Note:**Text") the other delimiter or an inline HTML tag
is used instead.
.TP
.BR \-\-code\-style =\fISTYLE\fR
.B fenced
(default, with the language taken from class names such as
.BR language\-python )
or
.B indented
code blocks.
.TP
.BR \-\-fence =\fICHAR\fR
Code fence character:
.B `
(default) or
.BR ~ .
.TP
.BR \-\-br\-style =\fISTYLE\fR
Hard line breaks as
.B backslash
(default) or two trailing
.BR spaces .
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wrap =\fICOLUMNS\fR
Wrap paragraphs, list items and block quotes at
.IR COLUMNS .
Lines are never broken inside link destinations or code, or where the new
line would start a different block construct.
.B 0
(default) disables wrapping.
.TP
.B \-\-compact\-tables
Do not pad table cells to align the columns.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-html
Never emit raw HTML. Superscripts, subscripts and keyboard input become
plain text or code, and line breaks in table cells become spaces.
.TP
.B \-\-preserve\-nbsp
Keep non\-breaking spaces (U+00A0) instead of converting them to ordinary
spaces.
.TP
.B \-\-front\-matter
Prepend YAML front matter with the document's title, description, author,
date, language and URL.
.SS Other
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress warnings.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.PP
Long options may be abbreviated to any unambiguous prefix, and enumerated
values may be abbreviated likewise (for example
.BR \-\-fla=common ).
.SH SELECTORS
Selectors support type, universal (*), #id, .class and attribute
selectors ([a], [a=v], [a~=v], [a|=v], [a^=v], [a$=v], [a*=v], with an
optional " i" flag), the pseudo\-classes :not(), :is(), :where(),
:first\-child, :last\-child, :only\-child and :empty, the descendant,
child (>), next\-sibling (+) and subsequent\-sibling (~) combinators, and
comma\-separated lists.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
When a document converts to nothing (or almost nothing) although it contains
text, html2md writes a warning to standard error naming the rule that removed
the text and the option that keeps it, for example when every section of a
page sits in a collapsed, hidden accordion panel. The exit status stays 0;
.B \-q
suppresses the message.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
All inputs were converted.
.TP
.B 1
An input could not be read or an output could not be written. Remaining
inputs are still processed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert a saved page:
.PP
.RS
html2md page.html > page.md
.RE
.PP
Download a page and keep only its article, with absolute links:
.PP
.RS
curl \-s https://example.com/post | html2md \-m \-b https://example.com/post
.RE
.PP
Convert every article of a page, without share buttons and ads, using
reference links:
.PP
.RS
html2md \-s article \-x '.share, .ad' \-\-links=reference index.html
.RE
.PP
Convert a directory of HTML files:
.PP
.RS
html2md \-d notes/ exported/*.html
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
The CommonMark specification: https://spec.commonmark.org/
.br
GitHub Flavored Markdown: https://github.github.com/gfm/
